# What the SOURCE distribution carries beyond the package itself.
#
# The wheel installs `db_ops/` and nothing else, so `pip install dbabrain` leaves a reader with no
# reference documentation at all - measured 2026-09-08 on a clean install, where the directory held
# `.venv` and nothing more. `dbabrain guide` answers the getting-started half without a network,
# and this answers the rest for anyone who takes the sdist.
#
# It is deliberately not the whole fix. Getting `docs/` into the WHEEL means relocating it under
# the package, and 121 places in this tree reference `docs/` by its current path; that is a
# refactor with its own review, not a line in a packaging file.
include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include LICENSE
include NOTICE
recursive-include docs *.md

# The worked examples, and the showcase of real published pages inside them. Added for 0.15.0,
# when the operator ruled that `examples/` ships with every public release: a reader who takes the
# sdist gets the two quickstart tool roots, the walkthroughs, and an actual estate's reports with
# every name replaced - which is the only honest way to show what the output looks like.
recursive-include examples *
